Cloud Trigger, which

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:44.780
will fire this process any
time your code changes, what

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:49.400
it's doing is it's building
and deploying from repository.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.820
So Buildpacks understand
specific language setups,

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:56.390
like Python, and Java,
and Go, and some others.

00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:58.190
What it will do is
it's worked out,

00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:01.130
because you have
a Python setup, it

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:03.170
will use a Python environment.

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:05.090
It will install
your dependencies

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:08.060
that you have in your
requirements.txt.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:10.500
And then as the entry
point on your container,

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:14.510
it will run that command that
you specified in the Procfile.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:17.750
This Buildpack will build
the container for you,

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:20.450
and then that will
be the container

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:22.610
that Cloud Run deploys.

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:26.060
