You just need to tell it-- you
need to use a standard language

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:52.950
that it understands implicitly.

00:10:52.950 --> 00:10:57.860
So it understands, for Java, how
to install Java dependencies;

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:00.273
for Python, how to install
Python dependencies.

00:11:00.273 --> 00:11:02.690
But it doesn't know how to run
your service, because there

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:05.940
are so many different ways that
you could start a web server.

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:08.300
So that's why you need
to tell it explicitly

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:10.210
when you want to
start my web server,

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:11.990
here is the command
that you want to run.

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:15.500
And in your case,
it was run flask.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:16.400
MARTIN: Oh, right.

