00:13:57.620 --> 00:13:59.780
And you can see the steps there.

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:02.570
The first step is Buildpack,
which builds the container.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:05.550
The second one is push,
which pushes the container.

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:07.070
And then the third
one is deploy.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:10.940
That will use that container
and then redeploy your service.

00:14:10.940 --> 00:14:13.400
And this is going to
happen any time you update

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.820
the main branch on your repo.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:18.890
So you can edit in VS
Code and push it up.

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:21.230
You can edit it in the
command line and push it up.

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:23.870
You can edit it
directly in GitHub.

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:27.620
Anywhere that will be a
commit on that main branch

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:29.530
of the remote repository.

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:32.030
So you have to remember to push
your code for it to trigger.

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:35.780
But anytime you edit
that code, this trigger

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:38.960
will redeploy everything.

